 "response": "Ruzapor's budget is now **$4,869K**.\n\n**Method**\n1. I counted only Finance Office records that change the budget. Messages from other departments and non-budget Finance notes (reminders, purchase orders, cost-center codes) were ignored.\n2. I resolved each chain of withdrawals starting from the latest one. A withdrawal counts only if it has not itself been withdrawn by a withdrawal that still counts.\n   - Example chain: #0241 withdraws #0142. That cancels #0142, so #0020 stands. #0020 withdraws #0014, so #0013 stands and cancels #0008. The +$391K in #0005 therefore applies.\n   - Example chain: #0214 withdraws #0133, so #0046 stands and cancels #0039. That leaves #0024 standing, which cancels #0021. So #0007 is withdrawn and its \u2212$447K does not apply.\n3. I started from the $2,560K set in #0001. Then I applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order, keeping a running total.\n\n**Checkpoints in the running total**\n- After #0019: $3,603K\n- After #0495: $4,438K\n- After #0690: $3,446K\n- After #1239: $4,384K\n- After #1335: $2,864K\n- After #1599: $4,869K\n\nThe total depends on summing roughly 500 entries by hand. A slip in one addition or one withdrawal chain would change the result.\n\nANSWER: $4869K",
